   "id": "renal-urology-red-flags",
   "title": "Renal and urological red flags",
   "target": "sys_examination",
   "alert": "Renal or urological emergency: send to emergency care now for potassium, creatinine and ECG. An infected obstructed kidney needs urgent decompression (stent or nephrostomy); catheterise acute or clot retention; anuria, hyperkalaemia, fluid overload or PD peritonitis need same-day nephrology review.",
