 "advice": [
  {
   "id": "kidney-protection",
   "title": "Looking after your kidneys",
   "target": "diet_lifestyle_advice",
   "text": "Keep active, aiming for at least 150 minutes of moderate activity a week if you are able. Do not smoke or chew tobacco. Keep salt below 5 g a day (about one level teaspoon in total), and cut down pickles, papads and packaged foods. Eat more vegetables and pulses. Do not take painkillers bought from a shop, or herbal or traditional remedies, without asking your doctor, as some can harm the kidneys."
  },
  {
   "id": "stone-prevention",
   "title": "Preventing kidney stones",
   "target": "diet_lifestyle_advice",
   "text": "Drink enough fluid, mostly water, spread through the day to pass about 2 to 2.5 litres of urine a day; drink more in hot weather or when you sweat a lot. Keep salt to 4 to 5 g a day and do not eat large amounts of meat, fish or eggs. Do not cut out milk and curd: a normal amount of calcium in the diet is advised. Keep a healthy weight and cut down sugary drinks and alcohol."
  },
  {
   "id": "urinary-symptoms-self-help",
   "title": "Helping urinary symptoms",
   "target": "diet_lifestyle_advice",
   "text": "Drink less in the evening and before going out, but do not cut your total fluids too much. Cut down tea, coffee and alcohol. Take your time and try passing urine a second time before leaving the toilet. When you get a sudden urge, try to hold on a little longer to train your bladder. Keep your bowels regular and tell your doctor about all the medicines you take."
  },
  {
   "id": "urology-warning-signs",
   "title": "Kidney and urine warning signs",
   "target": "follow_up_advice",
   "text": "Come to hospital at once if you cannot pass urine or pass very little, pass blood clots, have fever with shivering and pain in the side or back, have severe pain with vomiting, feel very weak or have palpitations, or become breathless. If you are on dialysis, also come at once if the fistula stops buzzing or the PD fluid turns cloudy."
  }
 ],
